{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.11", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:version-negotiation.9", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:open/field:max-frame-size.1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "a well-formed header for a version this peer does not speak", "start": "START", "steps": [{"bytes": "414d515000010100", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "unsupported", "state": "END", "status": "refused"}, "note": "major one minor one is a version this peer does not speak; the artifact states 1.0.0 and the peer supports exactly what the artifact states"}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "illegalState", "state": "END", "status": "refused"}, "note": "END's legal receives are `-`: the connection is over, so not even a header arrives on it"}], "vector": "exchange-header-version-unsupported"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.11", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:version-negotiation.12"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "a truncated protocol header: fewer octets than the layout's fixed width, which is a different failure from a header whose bytes mean nothing", "start": "START", "steps": [{"bytes": "414d5150000100", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "truncated", "state": "END", "status": "refused"}, "note": "seven octets where the header is eight"}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "illegalState", "state": "END", "status": "refused"}, "note": "END's legal receives are `-`: the connection is over, so not even a header arrives on it"}], "vector": "exchange-header-truncated"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.11", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:version-negotiation.12"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "octets that are not a protocol header at all: the ambiguity register's malformed, as distinct from a header for a protocol or version this peer does not speak", "start": "START", "steps": [{"bytes": "4854435000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "malformed", "state": "END", "status": "refused"}, "note": "the version negotiation example's HTTP case: eight octets that are not a protocol header, so the negotiation fails before any version can be compared"}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "illegalState", "state": "END", "status": "refused"}, "note": "END's legal receives are `-`: the connection is over, so not even a header arrives on it"}], "vector": "exchange-header-malformed"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:version-negotiation.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:connections.1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "an open offered before the header exchange: the octets are a legal open frame and the moment is wrong", "start": "START", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "illegalState", "state": "START", "status": "refused"}, "note": "the first frame on a connection is the open, but the protocol header precedes every frame, and START's legal send is HDR alone", "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 16}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "client", "type": "string"}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 0, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "HDR_SENT", "status": "admitted"}}], "vector": "exchange-open-before-header"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:version-negotiation.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:connections.2"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "a second open: admitted by a reading that takes `**` for `*`, refused by the artifact's rule that the first frame is the open", "start": "HDR_EXCH", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "OPEN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 16}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "client", "type": "string"}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 0, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "illegalState", "state": "OPEN_SENT", "status": "refused"}, "note": "the table's OPEN_SENT column is `**`, and a second open is not a frame known a priori to conform: the open is the first frame a peer sends, once", "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 16}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "client", "type": "string"}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 0, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}], "vector": "exchange-open-twice"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:connections.2"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "an open offered on channel one: legal octets, wrong channel", "start": "HDR_EXCH", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "illegalState", "state": "HDR_EXCH", "status": "refused"}, "note": "the open frame can only be sent on channel 0", "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 16}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "client", "type": "string"}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "OPEN_SENT", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 16}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "client", "type": "string"}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 0, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}], "vector": "exchange-open-on-channel-one-send"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:connections.2", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:open/field:channel-max.2"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "the same rule in the receive direction, where the consequence is the error-triggered close of the DISCARDING state", "start": "HDR_EXCH", "steps": [{"bytes": "0000001602000001005310c00901a106636c69656e74", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "illegalState", "state": "DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}, "note": "a received open on channel one: the connection is in error, so the peer closes and then discards what arrives until the partner's close"}, {"bytes": "0000000c0200000000531145", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"status": "admitted"}}], "vector": "exchange-open-on-channel-one-receive"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:version-negotiation.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:version-negotiation.12"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "a frame where the header belongs: the octets parse as a frame perfectly well, which is exactly why the failure is named by what was expected rather than by what arrived", "start": "START", "steps": [{"bytes": "0000001602000000005310c00901a106636c69656e74", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "malformed", "state": "END", "status": "refused"}, "note": "START's legal receive is the protocol header, so these octets \u2014 a frame \u2014 are not a header, and that is what the refusal reports"}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "illegalState", "state": "END", "status": "refused"}, "note": "END's legal receives are `-`: the connection is over, so not even a header arrives on it"}], "vector": "exchange-frame-where-header-belongs"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.23", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:version-negotiation.3"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "the header exchange happens once: a second header in HDR_RCVD is refused although its octets are identical to the first", "start": "START", "steps": [{"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "HDR_RCVD", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "414d515000010000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "illegalState", "state": "DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}, "note": "HDR_RCVD's legal receive is OPEN: a second header is not a frame the state permits, and nothing is sent twice"}], "vector": "exchange-two-headers"}
